<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Seeing ability: the eye. It holds the newest view of each
  source, asks the vision service how much a view changed since the last
  view of that source it handed on, and hands on a view that changed past a
  threshold; asked to look, it hands on every fresh view. The body
  (bots/floppy/floppy.scx) invokes it as its child "seeing" beside its
  other abilities, and its seeing_enabled switch decides whether it
  perceives (decision D189): on, it is an expected ability, every
  environment.visual goes to it after the input abilities and its look
  offer is taken; off, it is sent no stimulus and its offers are not taken.

    initializing -refused-> degraded (final)
                 -else-> perceiving
    perceiving { watching -environment.visual or look-> next
                 next -look pending-> interpreting
                      -an unmeasured fresh view-> measuring
                      -else-> watching
                 measuring -salient measurement-> interpreting
                           -below threshold, failure or timeout-> pacing
                 pacing -measure_every_ms or look-> next
                 interpreting { viewing -> objects_stage -> (detecting
                   -> detected) -> description_stage -> (describing) ->
                   viewed -> viewing ... -> handing_on } -sight-> settling
                 settling -settle_after_ms-> next }

  Initializing (decision D185) checks the invoker's <param>s before the eye
  perceives and refuses a change_threshold outside (0, 1], a duration that
  is not positive (measure_every_ms, measure_timeout_ms, settle_after_ms,
  max_view_age_ms, stage_timeout_ms), a measure_every_ms longer than
  settle_after_ms, and a measure that is neither byte_identity nor
  frame_diff. The first refusal, in that order, ends Seeing in the final
  state degraded, logged as seeing.degraded with its closed reason, so its
  invoker gets done.invoke.seeing. Otherwise initializing goes on to
  perceiving. Seeing attaches no children: each stage invokes its child for
  one view, and invoke lifecycle starts and cancels it (decision D6), so
  Seeing has no persistent child to wait for.

  Holding: environment.visual {image, media_type, kind, source,
  participants} is taken from wherever perception is, without interrupting
  it. Views older than max_view_age_ms (60 s) expire first; a stimulus
  without a source is then dropped (a view is keyed by its transducer);
  else it replaces its source's view (latest wins, moved to the newest
  place: views is in receipt order) unmeasured, keeping the source's
  measured_at; past four views (MAX_VIEWS) the least recently received is
  evicted. An expired or evicted source's seen signature is forgotten with
  it. Each outcome is logged (seeing.view: expired, dropped, held,
  evicted). Times are Date.now(), the session's clock, read once per hold
  and once per choice (next's chosen_at, which its choice, the look's
  request and the measured pick share).

  Looking: bot.ability.seeing.look {} is taken from wherever perception
  is and only remembered (look_pending); looks waiting for the same
  opportunity are one look. In watching and pacing it goes to next, and
  everywhere else it waits for the state to end, so every sight is
  followed by a full settle_after_ms (5 s).

  next chooses what comes next: a pending look goes first, ahead of any
  measurement, so motion cannot starve it: its request is every fresh view,
  newest first (ties in receipt order), each with change null and its
  age_ms, from source "seeing" (Seeing itself). Else an unmeasured fresh
  view is measured; else the eye watches.

  Measuring (the vision service, decision D185): measuring picks the least
  recently measured source among the unmeasured fresh views (never measured
  first, ties to the oldest arrival: a round robin), marks it measured now,
  and invokes the vision service ("vision") with measure (byte_identity,
  the default, or frame_diff), the view's image and the signature last
  handed on for its source (null for a first view). Its done data, a
  measurement {change, signature}, becomes
  bot.ability.seeing.measure.completed {source, visual, received_at,
  measurement} sent to itself: a change that is null (a first view) or at
  least change_threshold (0.1) is handed on (seeing.measure first or
  salient), the signature kept for its source while the source is still
  held, as the change request of that one view; a smaller change is not
  (below_threshold), and the signature handed on before stays, so drift
  keeps accumulating against it. A service that cannot measure (its start
  is rejected: error.execution), done data that is no measurement, and the
  measure_timeout_ms timer (2 s) become bot.ability.seeing.measure.failed
  {kind: measure_failed or timeout, message} sent to itself (seeing.measure
  failed or timeout): nothing is handed on, no other measure is asked, and
  a look still sees the view. Each measurement is followed by pacing,
  measure_every_ms (500 ms), so at most one measurement runs per
  measure_every_ms whatever the frame rate; frames in between only replace
  the held view.

  Interpreting (decision D187): the request's views are interpreted one
  after another, each by its objects stage and then its description stage
  (there is no face stage, decision D188). A stage whose switch is off
  (detect, describe; both false by default, so by default no stage runs) is
  passed at once; a stage that is on invokes its child for the view
  (detecting: abilities/object_detection/object_detection.scx as
  "object_detection"; describing: abilities/description/description.scx as
  "description"; each given the view's image and media_type and the model),
  bounded by stage_timeout_ms (30 s). Its output fills the view's objects
  or description; its bot.ability.failed, an error, or the timer leaves the
  field null. Each stage logs seeing.stage "<stage> ok", "<stage> failed"
  or "<stage> timeout". Leaving the stage's state cancels its child and its
  model call (SCXML 6.4), so no stage is left running (decision D186). What
  a cancelled child queued before its cancel is still delivered (W3C case
  236), and both children answer bot.ability.failed, so a stage's end
  drains: detected and viewed each send themselves an event (no delay,
  correlated by its sendid) and wait for it, so whatever the child queued
  before is dropped there, never taken as the next stage's answer. A
  child's done.invoke is not taken.

  Handing on: when every view is interpreted the eye sends itself
  bot.ability.seeing.sight {cause, views, participants} (participants the
  views' stamped participants, first occurrence first, at most 32), and the
  transition taking it sends the body bot.ability.cognition.input
  {stimulus: {event: "bot.ability.seeing.sight", data, source},
  participants} (source the view's source for a change, "seeing" for a
  look), logs seeing.sight (its cause) and settles: settling waits
  settle_after_ms, so at most one sight per settle_after_ms, plus
  deliberate looks.

  Offers: the entry into perceiving sends bot.ability.offers {ability:
  "seeing", choices} to the body: <decision:choice
  events="bot.ability.seeing.look"> (its one model-callable event), made
  model-facing by <processing:model_facing_schema> ($schema, title and
  examples dropped; over 32 KiB descriptions dropped too; still over, the
  offer is empty and logged).

  Logs (closed values only; never a source, a reference, a label, a
  description or a signature): seeing.degraded, seeing.view,
  seeing.measure, seeing.stage and seeing.sight, as above.

  Contracts: the events it takes reference abilities/schemas/ by
  event:schema (never inline), its own measure.completed, measure.failed
  and sight included, so a send whose data a schema rejects raises
  error.execution here. The vision service's done data is not checked by
  scxml.rs, so its cond checks its shape; the salience cond compares the
  change with change_threshold; the timers' conds correlate by sendid
  (decision D81). Each state's invoke is literal: a measure cancelled by
  its timer leaves measuring for pacing, where anything it queued before
  its cancel is dropped, and a stage child's leftovers are dropped in
  detected or viewed.

  Bindings: the decision and processing namespace packages and the vision
  service package; the stage children bind the generate service. The run
  grants the vision service the media directory it reads the views from
  as /media (scx run's dir option; bots/floppy/README.md gives it).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="Seeing" initial="initializing">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The invoker's <param>s, at their defaults. -->
    <data id="change_threshold" expr="0.1"/>
    <data id="measure" expr="'byte_identity'"/>
    <data id="measure_every_ms" expr="500"/>
    <data id="measure_timeout_ms" expr="2000"/>
    <data id="settle_after_ms" expr="5000"/>
    <data id="max_view_age_ms" expr="60000"/>
    <data id="stage_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="detect" expr="false"/>
    <data id="describe" expr="false"/>
    <data id="model" expr="'Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next'"/>
    <!-- The held views, in receipt order: {source, visual, received_at,
         measured, measured_at}; the signature last handed on per source,
         {source, signature}; and whether a look is waiting. -->
    <data id="views" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="seen" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="look_pending" expr="false"/>
    <!-- A hold, {views, outcomes, forgotten}: its outcomes, and the one
         being logged. -->
    <data id="held" expr="null"/>
    <data id="outcomes" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="outcome" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The time of next's choice, and the view being measured: {source,
         visual, received_at}. -->
    <data id="chosen_at" expr="0"/>
    <data id="measured" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The interpretation in hand: {cause, source, views}, and its view. -->
    <data id="request" expr="null"/>
    <data id="view_index" expr="0"/>
    <!-- The timer in hand. -->
    <data id="timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The offers. -->
    <data id="offered" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="offers_over" expr="false"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="seeing.js"/>

  <!-- The parameter refusals, in order: the first ends in degraded. -->
  <state id="initializing">
    <transition cond="refusesChangeThreshold()" target="degraded">
      <log label="seeing.degraded" expr="'change_threshold must be in (0, 1]'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="refusesDuration()" target="degraded">
      <log label="seeing.degraded" expr="refusedDurationReason()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="refusesPacing()" target="degraded">
      <log label="seeing.degraded" expr="'measure_every_ms cannot be longer than settle_after_ms'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="refusesMeasure()" target="degraded">
      <log label="seeing.degraded" expr="'measure must be byte_identity or frame_diff'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition target="perceiving"/>
  </state>

  <state id="perceiving" initial="watching">
    <onentry>
      <decision:choice location="offered" events="bot.ability.seeing.look"/>
      <processing:model_facing_schema location="offered" bound="32768" overlocation="offers_over"/>
      <if cond="offers_over">
        <log label="seeing.offers.dropped" expr="'the offers are over 32768 bytes'"/>
      </if>
      <send event="bot.ability.offers" target="#_parent">
        <param name="ability" expr="'seeing'"/>
        <param name="choices" expr="offered"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <!-- Wherever perception is, the newest frame replaces the held view
         and a look is remembered; neither interrupts what the eye is
         doing. -->
    <transition event="environment.visual" event:schema="../schemas/environment.visual.json">
      <assign location="held" expr="hold(_event)"/>
      <assign location="outcomes" expr="held.outcomes"/>
      <assign location="seen" expr="seenWithout(held.forgotten)"/>
      <assign location="views" expr="held.views"/>
      <foreach array="outcomes" item="outcome">
        <log label="seeing.view" expr="outcome"/>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.look" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.look.json">
      <assign location="look_pending" expr="true"/>
    </transition>

    <state id="watching">
      <transition event="environment.visual" event:schema="../schemas/environment.visual.json" target="next">
        <assign location="held" expr="hold(_event)"/>
        <assign location="outcomes" expr="held.outcomes"/>
        <assign location="seen" expr="seenWithout(held.forgotten)"/>
        <assign location="views" expr="held.views"/>
        <foreach array="outcomes" item="outcome">
          <log label="seeing.view" expr="outcome"/>
        </foreach>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.look" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.look.json" target="next">
        <assign location="look_pending" expr="true"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The next choice: a pending look goes first. -->
    <state id="next">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="chosen_at" expr="clockNow()"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition cond="look_pending" target="interpreting">
        <assign location="look_pending" expr="false"/>
        <assign location="request" expr="lookRequest()"/>
      </transition>
      <transition cond="hasUnmeasuredView()" target="measuring"/>
      <transition target="watching"/>
    </state>

    <!-- The least recently measured source's newest view, against the
         signature last handed on for it. -->
    <state id="measuring">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="measured" expr="measurePick()"/>
        <assign location="views" expr="markedMeasured()"/>
        <send idlocation="timer" event="measuring.after" delayexpr="delay(measure_timeout_ms)"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke id="vision" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/vision">
        <param name="measure" expr="measure"/>
        <param name="image" expr="measuredImage()"/>
        <param name="previous" expr="previousSignature()"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="done.invoke.vision" cond="isMeasurement(_event)">
        <send event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.completed" target="#_internal">
          <param name="source" expr="measured.source"/>
          <param name="visual" expr="measured.visual"/>
          <param name="received_at" expr="measured.received_at"/>
          <param name="measurement" expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.vision">
        <send event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.failed" target="#_internal">
          <param name="kind" expr="'measure_failed'"/>
          <param name="message" expr="'the vision service answered no measurement'"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*">
        <send event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.failed" target="#_internal">
          <param name="kind" expr="'measure_failed'"/>
          <param name="message" expr="measureCouldNotRunMessage(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="measuring.after" cond="isTimer(_event)">
        <send event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.failed" target="#_internal">
          <param name="kind" expr="'timeout'"/>
          <param name="message" expr="measureTimedOutMessage()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.completed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.measure.completed.json"
                  cond="isSalient(_event)" target="interpreting">
        <log label="seeing.measure" expr="salience(_event)"/>
        <assign location="seen" expr="seenAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="request" expr="changeRequest(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.completed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.measure.completed.json"
                  target="pacing">
        <log label="seeing.measure" expr="'below_threshold'"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.measure.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.measure.failed.json"
                  target="pacing">
        <log label="seeing.measure" expr="measureFailedOutcome(_event)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- At most one measurement per measure_every_ms, whatever the
         source's frame rate. -->
    <state id="pacing">
      <onentry>
        <send idlocation="timer" event="pacing.after" delayexpr="delay(measure_every_ms)"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="pacing.after" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="next"/>
      <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.look" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.look.json" target="next">
        <assign location="look_pending" expr="true"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- What the requested views show, one view after another, then the
         sight. -->
    <state id="interpreting" initial="viewing">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="view_index" expr="0"/>
      </onentry>

      <state id="viewing">
        <transition cond="isViewLeft()" target="objects_stage"/>
        <transition target="handing_on"/>
      </state>

      <state id="objects_stage">
        <transition cond="detect" target="detecting"/>
        <transition target="description_stage"/>
      </state>

      <state id="detecting">
        <onentry>
          <send idlocation="timer" event="detecting.after" delayexpr="delay(stage_timeout_ms)"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="object_detection" type="scxml" src="../object_detection/object_detection.scx">
          <param name="image" expr="currentView().image"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="currentView().media_type"/>
          <param name="model" expr="model"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="bot.ability.vision.detection.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vision.detection.output.json"
                    target="detected">
          <assign location="request.views[view_index].objects" expr="_event.data.objects"/>
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'objects ok'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="detected">
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'objects failed'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="detected">
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'objects failed'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="detecting.after" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="detected">
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'objects timeout'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Whatever a cancelled stage child queued before its cancel is
           ahead of the drain on the external queue, so it is dropped here
           before the next stage starts. -->
      <state id="detected">
        <onentry>
          <send idlocation="timer" event="detected.drained"/>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="detected.drained" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="description_stage"/>
      </state>

      <state id="description_stage">
        <transition cond="describe" target="describing"/>
        <transition target="viewed"/>
      </state>

      <state id="describing">
        <onentry>
          <send idlocation="timer" event="describing.after" delayexpr="delay(stage_timeout_ms)"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="description" type="scxml" src="../description/description.scx">
          <param name="image" expr="currentView().image"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="currentView().media_type"/>
          <param name="model" expr="model"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="bot.ability.vision.description.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.vision.description.output.json"
                    target="viewed">
          <assign location="request.views[view_index].description" expr="_event.data.description"/>
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'description ok'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="viewed">
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'description failed'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="viewed">
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'description failed'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="describing.after" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="viewed">
          <log label="seeing.stage" expr="'description timeout'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- As detected: the description child's leftovers are dropped
           before the next view's stages start. -->
      <state id="viewed">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="view_index" expr="nextViewIndex()"/>
          <send idlocation="timer" event="viewed.drained"/>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="viewed.drained" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="viewing"/>
      </state>

      <!-- The sight, through this ability's terminal: the body's turn. -->
      <state id="handing_on">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.seeing.sight" target="#_internal">
            <param name="cause" expr="request.cause"/>
            <param name="views" expr="request.views"/>
            <param name="participants" expr="sightParticipants()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.seeing.sight" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.seeing.sight.json" target="settling">
          <log label="seeing.sight" expr="_event.data.cause"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
            <param name="stimulus" expr="sightStimulus(_event)"/>
            <param name="participants" expr="_event.data.participants"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- A sight its schema refuses is not handed on (its views come
             from schema-checked events, so this is a backstop). -->
        <transition event="error.*" target="settling">
          <log label="seeing.sight" expr="'failed'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
    </state>

    <!-- Every sight is followed by a full settle_after_ms: at most one per
         settle_after_ms, plus looks. -->
    <state id="settling">
      <onentry>
        <send idlocation="timer" event="settling.after" delayexpr="delay(settle_after_ms)"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="settling.after" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="next"/>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- A refused configuration: Seeing ends, and its invoker gets
       done.invoke.seeing. -->
  <final id="degraded"/>
</scxml>
